Make-Blog "how-to-download-ntn-certificate-fbr" "How to Download NTN Certificate from FBR IRIS 2026" "Step-by-step guide to download your NTN certificate from FBR IRIS portal in Pakistan 2026. How to print or save your National Tax Number certificate online." "2027-04-06" "FBR Guide" '<p class="article-lead">Your NTN (National Tax Number) certificate is an official document issued by FBR confirming your tax registration. This guide shows exactly how to download and print your NTN certificate from the FBR IRIS portal in 2026. If you need help obtaining or registering your NTN, Kamboh Associates handles it in 24-48 hours.</p><h2 id="overview">What is an NTN Certificate?</h2><p>An NTN certificate is a formal document issued by FBR confirming your registration in the national tax system. For individuals, your NTN is the same as your CNIC number. The NTN certificate is required for opening business bank accounts, registering a business, tendering for government contracts, and many other official purposes.</p><h2 id="obligations">How to Download NTN Certificate from FBR IRIS</h2><ol><li><strong>Login to FBR IRIS</strong> - Go to iris.fbr.gov.pk and enter your CNIC/NTN and password</li><li><strong>Go to Registration</strong> - In the left menu, click "Registration" then select "114(1) Registration"</li><li><strong>Open Your Profile</strong> - Your registered taxpayer profile opens showing your NTN, name, address, and registration details</li><li><strong>Print or Download</strong> - Click the print icon or use your browser''s print function (Ctrl+P) to save as PDF or print the certificate</li><li><strong>Official Stamp Version</strong> - For official stamped copies, visit your nearest FBR Tax Facilitation Centre with your CNIC</li></ol><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Alternative Method:</strong> You can also verify and view your NTN details on the FBR Active Taxpayer portal. For a certified hard copy with FBR stamp, visit any FBR facilitation centre or Regional Tax Office (RTO) with your CNIC.</p></div><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Forgot IRIS Password?</strong> Click "Forgot Password" on the IRIS login page and enter your CNIC. A reset code is sent to your registered mobile. If your mobile number has changed, WhatsApp 0328-4675162 and we help you recover access.</p></div><h2 id="services">NTN Registration Services</h2><ul><li><strong>New NTN Registration</strong> - Completed in 24-48 hours for individuals and businesses</li><li><strong>NTN for Companies</strong> - SECP-registered company NTN with all required documents</li><li><strong>NTN Recovery</strong> - Retrieve lost or forgotten NTN credentials</li><li><strong>Profile Update</strong> - Change address, phone, or email in FBR records</li></ul><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Individual NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>24-48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Business NTN Registration</td><td>From Rs 3,000</td><td>2-3 days</td></tr><tr><td>NTN Profile Update</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Need Your NTN? We Register It in 24 Hours</h3><p>WhatsApp your CNIC copy to 0328-4675162. We complete FBR IRIS registration and send you your NTN same day.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+need+NTN+registration+or+certificate+download+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Get NTN Now</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Is my NTN the same as my CNIC? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. For individual taxpayers in Pakistan, the NTN is the same as your 13-digit CNIC number. You do not receive a separate NTN number - your CNIC is your tax identifier after e-enrollment on FBR IRIS.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How do I get a stamped NTN certificate from FBR? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Visit any FBR Tax Facilitation Centre or Regional Tax Office (RTO) with your original CNIC. They issue a stamped and signed NTN certificate on the spot. You can find the nearest facilitation centre on the FBR website.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">I cannot login to FBR IRIS to download my certificate. What should I do? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">WhatsApp your CNIC to 0328-4675162. Kamboh Associates retrieves your NTN credentials, resets your IRIS access, and provides your certificate details. We handle complete NTN recovery.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "how-to-reset-fbr-iris-password" "How to Reset FBR IRIS Password in Pakistan 2026" "Step-by-step guide to reset forgotten FBR IRIS password in Pakistan 2026. How to recover IRIS login, change password, update mobile number on FBR portal." "2027-04-07" "FBR Guide" '<p class="article-lead">Forgotten your FBR IRIS password? This guide shows exactly how to reset it in 2026. There are three methods depending on whether you have access to your registered mobile number. If all methods fail, Kamboh Associates can recover your IRIS access for you.</p><h2 id="overview">Method 1: Reset via Registered Mobile Number (Fastest)</h2><ol><li>Go to <strong>iris.fbr.gov.pk</strong></li><li>Click <strong>"Forgot Password"</strong> on the login page</li><li>Enter your CNIC number (13 digits)</li><li>A 6-digit OTP is sent to your registered mobile number</li><li>Enter the OTP and set a new password</li><li>Password must be at least 8 characters with a mix of letters, numbers, and symbols</li></ol><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Password Requirements:</strong> FBR IRIS passwords must be 8+ characters and include at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, one number, and one special character (e.g., @, #, $). Common passwords are rejected.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Method 2: Mobile Number Changed or Not Accessible</h2><p>If you no longer have access to your registered mobile number, you must update it through FBR directly. Two options:</p><ul><li><strong>Visit FBR Facilitation Centre:</strong> Bring your original CNIC to any FBR Tax Facilitation Centre or RTO. They update your mobile number and reset your access on the spot.</li><li><strong>FBR Helpline:</strong> Call 051-111-772-772 and request a mobile number update. You will be asked security questions to verify identity.</li><li><strong>Use Kamboh Associates:</strong> WhatsApp 0328-4675162 with your CNIC. We handle IRIS credential recovery without requiring you to visit FBR in person.</li></ul><h2 id="services">Method 3: Email-Based Reset</h2><ol><li>On the IRIS login page, click "Forgot Password"</li><li>Enter your CNIC and select "Send to Email" if that option appears</li><li>Check your registered email inbox for the reset link</li><li>Click the link and set a new password within 30 minutes</li></ol><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Account Locked?</strong> After 5 failed login attempts, FBR IRIS locks your account for 24 hours. Wait 24 hours before attempting to reset, or contact FBR helpline immediately to unlock early.</p></div><h2 id="pricing">IRIS Recovery by Kamboh Associates</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>IRIS Password Reset Assistance</td><td>From Rs 1,000</td><td>Same day</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile Number Update on IRIS</td><td>From Rs 1,500</td><td>1-2 days</td></tr><tr><td>Full IRIS Account Recovery</td><td>From Rs 2,000</td><td>1-3 days</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Cannot Access IRIS? We Recover It For You</h3><p>WhatsApp 0328-4675162 with your CNIC. Kamboh Associates handles IRIS password reset and account recovery.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+forgot+my+FBR+IRIS+password+and+need+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Get Help Now</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What if I don''t remember which mobile number is registered on FBR IRIS? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Visit any FBR Tax Facilitation Centre with your original CNIC. They can look up your registered mobile number and update it. Alternatively, WhatsApp 0328-4675162 - Kamboh Associates can verify and update your registered contact details.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">How long does it take to reset FBR IRIS password? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">If you have access to your registered mobile, reset takes under 5 minutes via OTP. If your mobile number needs updating, plan for 1-2 business days for FBR to process the change.</div></div></div>'

Make-Blog "how-to-respond-fbr-notice-section-111" "How to Respond to FBR Section 111 Notice in Pakistan 2026" "Complete guide on how to respond to FBR Section 111 notice in Pakistan. What is Section 111, unexplained income notice, required documents, response deadline and process." "2027-04-08" "FBR Notices" "FBR Notice Guide" '<p class="article-lead">An FBR Section 111 notice is one of the most serious notices a taxpayer can receive. It requires you to explain the source of income or assets that FBR believes are unexplained. Ignoring this notice can result in additional tax assessments, penalties, and prosecution. Kamboh Associates responds to Section 111 notices professionally on your behalf.</p><h2 id="overview">What is FBR Section 111?</h2><p>Section 111 of the Income Tax Ordinance 2001 deals with unexplained income, assets, investments, or expenditure. FBR issues a Section 111 notice when their data systems detect that your declared income does not match your observed lifestyle, assets, or financial transactions. Common triggers include property purchases, vehicle registrations, large bank deposits, or foreign remittances that do not match your declared income.</p><div class="warn-box"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i><p><strong>Do Not Ignore This Notice:</strong> A Section 111 notice has a specific response deadline, typically 30 days. If you fail to respond or provide insufficient explanation, FBR can add the unexplained amount to your taxable income and assess additional tax plus 100% penalty under Section 182.</p></div><h2 id="obligations">Common Reasons for Section 111 Notice</h2><ul><li><strong>Property Purchase</strong> - Buying property worth more than declared income suggests</li><li><strong>Vehicle Registration</strong> - Registering an expensive vehicle without matching income</li><li><strong>Large Bank Deposits</strong> - Cash deposits not matching declared income</li><li><strong>Foreign Remittances</strong> - Receiving large remittances without explanation</li><li><strong>Investment in Business</strong> - Capital invested in a business not matching declared savings</li><li><strong>Lifestyle Expenditure</strong> - Overseas travel, school fees, rent paid - all cross-checked by FBR</li></ul><h2 id="services">How to Respond to Section 111 Notice</h2><ol><li><strong>Read the Notice Carefully</strong> - Identify exactly what income/assets FBR is questioning and the specific tax year</li><li><strong>Gather Evidence</strong> - Collect documents proving the source: salary certificates, business receipts, inheritance documents, gift deeds, loan agreements, prior year savings</li><li><strong>File Written Reply</strong> - Submit a written reply through FBR IRIS under the relevant notice, attaching all supporting documents</li><li><strong>Attend Hearing if Called</strong> - FBR may call you for a hearing with the tax officer; attend with a qualified consultant</li><li><strong>Negotiate if Needed</strong> - In some cases, a negotiated settlement with supporting evidence is possible</li></ol><div class="info-box"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i><p><strong>Professional Help is Critical:</strong> Responding incorrectly or incompletely to a Section 111 notice can make the situation worse. Kamboh Associates has handled hundreds of FBR notices and prepares a strong, documented response on your behalf.</p></div><h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Section 111 Notice Response</td><td>From Rs 10,000</td><td>3-5 days</td></tr><tr><td>FBR Hearing Representation</td><td>From Rs 15,000</td><td>As scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>Assessment Appeal</td><td>From Rs 20,000</td><td>Case dependent</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="article-cta"><h3>Received Section 111 Notice? Act Now</h3><p>WhatsApp the notice to 0328-4675162 immediately. Kamboh Associates prepares your full reply before the deadline.</p><div class="cta-btns"><a href="https://wa.me/923284675162?text=Hi%2C+I+received+an+FBR+Section+111+notice+and+need+urgent+help." class="cta-btn-white" target="_blank"><i class="fab fa-whatsapp"></i> Get Help Urgently</a><a href="tel:03284675162" class="cta-btn-ghost"><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> 0328-4675162</a></div></div><h2 id="faqs">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What happens if I ignore an FBR Section 111 notice? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">If you ignore the notice, FBR will add the unexplained amount to your taxable income and issue an assessment order charging tax plus a 100% penalty under Section 182. In severe cases, prosecution under Section 192 is possible. Always respond before the deadline.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">What documents can I use to explain the source of funds for Section 111? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Acceptable evidence includes: prior year bank statements showing accumulated savings, salary certificates, business sale receipts, agricultural income evidence, loan agreements, gift deeds from family, inheritance documents, and foreign remittance certificates from the bank.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">Can FBR issue Section 111 for previous years? <i class="fas fa-plus"></i></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. FBR can examine tax years up to 5 years back under normal circumstances, and up to 10 years if fraud is suspected. Notices can be received for transactions made several years ago.</div></div></div>'

